<title>CHINA: Banque Indosuez moves branch to Shanghai's Pudong.</title>
<headline>Banque Indosuez moves branch to Shanghai's Pudong.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Banque Indosuez has moved its Shanghai branch to the city's Pudong area in preparation for beginning local currency business, the official Shanghai Securities News reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>China has approved nine foreign banks, including Banque Indosuez, to carry out yuan business but the banks must first relocate to Pudong, which the government is promoting as the country's premier financial and economic zone.</p>
</text>
